000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, MAY 7, 2008\r\rMayor Maurer called the meeting to order at 6:30 p.m. in Conference Room No. 2, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Maurer, Mayor pro Tem Wolfson, Councilmembers Bozajian, Groveman, Washburn.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles.\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rThe City Council recessed at 6:31 p.m. into closed session to confer with legal counsel regarding the following:\r\r1. One matter of Anticipated Litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section G.C. G.C. 54956.9b(3)(C), a point has been reached where, in the opinion of the City Council/Agency on the advice of its legal counsel, based on the below-described existing facts and circumstances, there is a significant exposure to litigation against the City Council/Agency: Receipt of Claim pursuant to Tort Claims Act or other written communication from Los Angeles Regional Water Quality Control Board Notice of Violation directed to Calabasas, Los Angeles County, and 19 other cities threatening litigation (copy available for public inspection in City Clerk�s office). \r2. Pending litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54946.9(a): Calabasas Ridge HOA v. Gordon, LC 079145; Smith v. City of Calabasas, BS 106644; Cooper v. Calabasas Park Estates Owners Association,�BC 323695; Toby Keeler & Elizabeth Stephens v. City of Calabasas, BS 109503; Parks v. City of Calabasas, BC 382012.\r\rThe City Council reconvened at 7:30 p.m. from closed session, and Mayor Maurer called the meeting to order at 7:40 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Maurer, Mayor pro Tem Wolfson, Councilmembers Bozajian, Groveman, Washburn.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Peirce, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Jimmie Cho.\r\rMichael G. Colantuono, City Attorney, stated that there was no reportable action in closed session.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Mayor pro Tem Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to approve the agenda with the continuance of Item #12. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS \r\rMayor Maurer introduced Jimmie Cho, the new Director of Resource Conservation and Public Outreach at the Las Virgenes Water Management District. Mayor Maurer introduced Myriah Harris, who presented a report from Conejo/Las Virgenes Future Foundation on the Annual Youth Congress. Mayor Maurer introduced Bob Milner, the new General Manager for Mercedes Benz of Calabasas. Councilmember Bozajian thanked and congratulated the Calabasas Arts Council and Laureen Morrick on the successful Arts Festival and announced the upcoming Calabasas Historical Society Annual BBQ. Councilmember Washburn spoke regarding the recent Anza en Calabasas Pageant. Mayor pro Tem Wolfson and Mayor Maurer congratulated and thanked the Arts Council and staff for the successful Arts Festival. Mayor Maurer spoke regarding the recent Creek Clean-up that occurred in conjunction with Big Sunday. Mayor pro Tem Wolfson announced that the Relay for Life event will be held on May 17 � 18, 2008.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r No one indicated a desire to speak.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of the minutes for the April 16, 2008 City Council meeting. \r\r Recommendation to award a professional services agreement to DMS Facility Services in the amount of $110,000 for facility engineering services for the Calabasas Civic Center. \r\r Recommendation to reject all bid proposals for the technology installation at the new Civic Center. \r\r Recommendation to approve a professional services agreement with AT&T in the amount not to exceed $218,215.50 to provide an IP-Based Voice Communications System for the Calabasas Civic Center. \r\r Recommendation to award a construction contract to Timothy J. Ferrie, Inc. in the amount of $400,000 for the Annual Citywide Concrete Rehabilitation, Specification No. 07-08-15. \r\r Recommendation to accept completion of the Las Virgenes Creek Restoration project, Specification No. 06-07-12 by Olivas Valdez, Inc.; and to direct the City Clerk to file the Notice of Completion. \r\r Recommendation to approve the nomination of Karen Brown by Mayor Maurer to the Library Commission. \r\r Recommendation to approve the purchase and installation of security gates for the new Calabasas Library from 3M Library Systems in the amount of $62,000. \r\r Authorization to extend Venco Western, Inc. contract completion date for one year, from May 3, 2008 to May 3, 2009 for Specification 05-06-02, Landscape Maintenance of the common areas within individual homeowners associations and common benefit areas with Landscape Maintenance District 22. \r\r Recommendation to award a construction contract to TDS Engineering in the amount of $228,500 for the Las Virgenes Road Corridor Signal Interconnect, Specification No. 07-08-16. \r\rCouncilmember Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to approve Consent Items #1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9 and 10. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rPUBLIC HEARING\r\r Introduction of Ordinance No. 2008-247, amending Chapter 22, affordable housing, of Title 17 of the Calabasas Municipal Code, to correct the inadvertent deletion of the affordable housing inclusionary requirements from Chapter 22 of Title 17 of the Calabasas Municipal Code. \r\r Mayor Maurer opened the public hearing.\r\r Tom Bartlett, City Planner, presented the staff report.\r\rMayor Maurer closed the public hearing.\r\rMayor pro Tem Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to introduce Ordinance No. 2008-247, amending Chapter 22, affordable housing, of Title 17 of the Calabasas Municipal Code, to correct the inadvertent deletion of the affordable housing inclusionary requirements from Chapter 22 of Title 17 of the Calabasas Municipal Code. MOTION CARRIED 4/1 with Councilmember Bozajian voting NO. \r\r Introduction of Ordinance No. 2008-248, approving the pre-zoning of the Mont Calabasas Annexation Area (Permit No. PL0800613) in conformance with the land use policies of the Calabasas General Plan and in preparation for submission of an application to the Los Angeles County Local Area Formation Commission seeking annexation of the Mont Calabasas area to the City of Calabasas. \r\rThis item was continued to the City Council meeting of May 21, 2008. \r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS\r\r Discussion of changes to the recreational vehicle ordinance.\r\rMaureen Tamuri, Community Development Director, presented the staff report.\r\rRachel Heller, Calabasas, Reed Vertelney, Calabasas, Martin Colbenz, Calabasas, Valerie Gebroe, Calabasas, Harry Preston, Calabasas, Emma Wilby, Calabasas, spoke in support of strengthening the restrictions on parking for recreational vehicles. Lucy Martin, President of the Greater Mulwood Homeowners Association, spoke in opposition to recreational vehicles parking on the street and in opposition to changing the current recreational vehicle ordinance. Dale Reicheneder, Vice President, Steeplechase Homeowners Association, Norm Buehring, President, Community Association of Saratoga Hills, spoke in support of staff�s recommendations with certain revisions. \r\rMayor pro Tem Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to draft a Streets and Highways ordinance comprising of expanding the definition of recreational vehicles and eliminating the 72 hour allowance of on-street parking in favor of no on-street parking with the exception of 1 day parking with permit. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rNEW BUSINESS \r\r Presentation by the Chief Financial Officer regarding the financial condition of the City.\r\rThere was no action taken.\r\r Discussion regarding water quality issues.\r\rMireille Neumann, expressed concern over water quality issues and spoke in support of the City not adopting laws and policies that promote growth.\r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS \r\r Check Register for the period of April 10, 2008 to April 24, 2008. \r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r Mayor Maurer provided information on the School Task Force. Mayor pro Tem Wolfson provided an update on the Civic Center Task Force.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r City Manager Coroalles indicated he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\r Councilmember Washburn requested that an item regarding putting together a task force to study comprehensive regional issues be placed on a future agenda.\r\rADJOURN \r\r The City Council adjourned at 10:07 p.m.\r\r\r\r\r__________________________________\rRobin Parker, City Clerk\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 4 -\u0015\r\r\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u0014- 4 -\u0015\r05/07/08\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0001\b\u0000\u0000\u0015\b\u0000\u0000\u0016\b\u0000\u0000#\b\u0000\u0000*\b\u0000\u0000q\b\u0000\u0000r\b\u0000\u0000w\b\u0000\u0000}\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000\u0005 \u0000\u0000\u000e \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000\u001e\n\u0000\u0000%\n\u0000\u00000\n\u0000\u0000���Ǹǭ���~�mcUcUcI:\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u001c\u0015h�\u0018 \u0000\u0016h�/\f\u0000OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000^J\u0003\u0000aJ\u0018\u0000\u0000\u0016\u0016h�/\f\u0000OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000^J\u0003\u0000aJ\u0018\u0000\u0000\u001b\u0016h�/\f\u00005\b�>*\u0001OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000\\\b�^J\u0003\u0000\u0012\u0016h�/\f\u0000OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000^J\u0003\u0000\u0000!\u0016h\u001a \u0018\u00005\b�>*\u0001B*\u0001OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000aJ\u0018\u0000ph\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0015\u0016h�\u0002�\u00005\b�OJ\u0003\u0000QJ\u0003\u0000aJ\